      "role": "EN-READ-F",
      "source": "reading.text",
      "tts_text": "The rowing group reached the shoreline after dusk and could not see the boathouse. A faint light appeared beyond a bed of reeds. One visitor believed that the beacon had flashed, but it was the keeper who had carried a lantern along the path. The wooden marker, not the map, showed the final turn. It was the lamplight that helped the group avoid the rocks near the cove. Once everyone was inside, the keeper explained that the beacon had failed earlier that evening. The next morning, the volunteers repaired it. The story was simple, but the group remembered exactly which light had guided them.",
